vectorwake (criccomini, push to main): Subspace-inspired MMO with own art. Deterministic C99 core, Rust authoritative server, Defold client; bots emit inputs only, damage-weighted Elo. Built through M5.5.                                                                                   
The client grew multiplayer, call signs and map files, and a silent build failure shipped three stale artifacts. Zones now own their rules and send them over the wire: one weapon model, a tech tree of levels and add-ons and charges, bounty derived from what you hold.                    
Matched the original wherever it actually specifies something (prize weights, multifire cost, weapon clocks, repel and burst), but it ships no per-ship balance, so the roster is ours. Mobile keeps the pointing stick and no reverse. Hosting is Vultr; cost is egress.                      
